rule: (process) reuse-established-notation-not-a-parallel-one -- templates/clean_engineering-sketch.md already defines the exact terse notation for this ("-> collaborator.operation" for an interaction, "// ..." for an invariant or sequencing note, nested under the calling operation); inventing a parallel "- **Interaction:** calls X.Y" / "- **Invariant:** [rule]" bold-bullet convention duplicates a symbol set that already exists in this same tool, instead of reusing it. Compounded by (process) do-not-invent-requirements: asked only to put the interactions in order (sequencing = bullet order), answered instead with invented loop-mechanics/resolution prose stuffed inside the invented bullet.
wrong: Added "### Interactions (optional at this fidelity)" / "### Invariants (optional at this fidelity)" to clean_engineering.md's ## model using a self-invented "- **Interaction:** calls {OtherClass}.{operation}" / "- **Invariant:** [rule]" bullet format, then applied it in the sketch with full parameter lists and iteration/resolution mechanics stuffed into the Interaction bullet (e.g. "calls CatalogAction.generate_catalog(action, owner) once per lifecycle-action name, in BaseContextTool's declared source order ..., each name resolved via owner.actions"). Two follow-up attempts to fix it kept the same invented bold-bullet shape instead of switching to the already-established "->"/"//" notation from templates/clean_engineering-sketch.md.
original: |
  clean_engineering.md: "- Name an interaction as a bullet on the calling
    class: **`- **Interaction:** calls {OtherClass}.{operation}`** -- no
    signature, no body ..."
  sketch.md (CatalogFidelity): "- **Interaction:** calls
    `CatalogAction.generate_catalog(action, owner)` once per lifecycle-action
    name, in `BaseContextTool`'s declared source order (`partition`, `grill`,
    `sketch`, `generate`, `document`, `iterate`, `validate`, `satisfy`,
    `repair`), each name resolved via `owner.actions` -- this is Section 0's
    nine hyperlinked actions."
improved: |
  clean_engineering.md now points at the real notation directly: "Reuse the
  exact notation from templates/{tool}-sketch.md's Notation/Interaction
  rules -- do not invent a parallel bullet convention. Nest
  -> {collaborator}.{operation} directly under the calling operation ...
  Nest // ... under the same operation for any invariant or sequencing note
  -- including looping/conditionals around the call."
  sketch.md's six classes now nest the real symbols under each
  generate_catalog operation inside its existing class-card fence, e.g.
  CatalogFidelity: "generate_catalog(fidelity_name, owner): str / ->
  catalog_action.generate_catalog / // once per lifecycle-action name, in
  BaseContextTool's declared source order (partition, grill, sketch,
  generate, document, iterate, validate, satisfy, repair) / // never mutates
  owner -- read-only render of a live object." Order of the -> lines is the
  whole of "sequencing."
