artifact: context_tools/stories/scanners/{behaviours_not_one_time_tasks,do_not_invent_requirements}_scanner.py + their examples/evals fixtures
rule: (process) scanner-only-for-mechanical-checks
wrong: Built regex/graph-based scanners (and faultyAsset/repairedAsset fixture pairs + verify_regression expectations) for two rules that are actually judgment calls, not mechanical patterns: `behaviours-not-one-time-tasks` (is this story a repeatable behaviour vs a one-time chore?) and `do-not-invent-requirements` (is this line grounded in source context or invented?). The latter's 'scanner' only worked by hardcoding the exact phrases from one incident's mistakes.log entries - not a generalizable mechanical check, just an overfit literal-text matcher dressed up as one.
original: |
  improve.md / repair.md assumed every corrected mistake needs a scanner + fixture pair + regression entry to close the loop, with no branch for rules that cannot be stated as a deterministic pattern.
improved: |
  Deleted both scanners and their examples/evals fixtures; kept only the prose rule bullets in stories.md / base_context_tool.md / templates/stories-sketch.md. Updated repair.md with a new 'Not every rule is a scanner rule' section: before building/editing a scanner, ask whether the violation is a deterministic pattern; if it is a judgment call, skip straight to root-cause + a prose-only fix, close on validate instead of scan, and skip fixture capture (Steps 1 and 6 now marked 'mechanical rules only'). Updated improve.md Steps 3-4 to match: a fixture pair and regression offer only happen when the rule is mechanical. Also fixed three unrelated infra bugs surfaced while getting verify_regression working at all: RegressionExample._paths() didn't recognize extensioned fixtures, Scanner.is_skipped_path checked the full filename instead of the stem, and Scan.scan() hardcoded Path.cwd() as scan root (causing a full-repo hang for graph-wide scanners and a path-doubling bug when paths were already root-relative).
status: fixed
